Note for the copyright holder
------------------------------

This file was written to reflect the decision to publish this project without
an open-source licence. It is a starting point and has NOT been reviewed by a
lawyer, which matters here for two specific reasons:

  - Several jurisdictions (notably Germany, and France for commercial terms)
    require certain mandatory consumer rights to be preserved in a proprietary
    licence. Restricting use entirely may not be enforceable against consumers
    in those places.
  - A repository published without a licence is, by default, "all rights
    reserved" — so the absence of a licence would already have had much of this
    effect. This file makes it explicit rather than implied, which is clearer
    for readers but does not add protection.

Get it reviewed before you rely on it commercially.